  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Humanitarian Integrated Food Income and Livelihoods Project (HI-FILP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Caritas intends to improve on the food, nutrition, and livelihood situations in 9 000 households (45 000 individuals) in Bidibidi Refugee Settlement and neighbouring host communities. The intervention includes promotion of climate smart agriculture production, value addition, skilling in income generating ventures and access to markets. The initiatives are designed to increase household incomes of women and girls, enabling acquisition of assets to curb vulnerability to future food insecurity crisis. The target group of the project is a total of 9000 households (70% female and 30% male-headed) households, 70% refugees and 30% in host communities, 5% (450) PWDs. For skills training the target group is girls and women between 15 and 30 years of age.</narrative>
  </description>
